# API keys for LOCAL runs. Cloud Routine runs need none of these here: the environment's
# API credentials add each key to requests for its host, so it never enters the session.
# RANSOMWARE_LIVE_API_KEY=  # ransomware.live API PRO (free key), sent as X-API-KEY
# HIBP_API_KEY=            # HaveIBeenPwned domain search (deferred); the breach catalogue
                           # the `hibp` collector reads needs no key
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=       # LLM triage/summary agent (Phase 2)

# --email flag: sends the digest only when there are alerts or a collector failure.
# SMTP_USER and EMAIL_TO are required. SMTP_PASSWORD is optional: if unset, it falls
# back to a macOS Keychain item (same technique as ~/.claude/hooks/email-notify.py) —
# reuses that Gmail App Password instead of duplicating it here. To add one directly:
#   security add-generic-password -a $USER -s claude-email-notify -w '<app password>'
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=              # optional — omit to use the Keychain fallback
# SMTP_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE=claude-email-notify
# EMAIL_FROM=                 # defaults to SMTP_USER if unset
# EMAIL_TO=you@example.com    # comma-separated for multiple recipients
